      "context": "Appendix III table giving the total population of Peking for 1913 to 1917, with male and female figures for 1915-17 and the percentage yearly increase, as part of the police-census population figures.",
      "transcriber_notes": [
        "Rows: 6 as printed (5 years + Total increase). Printed rules (dashes) in the 1913/1914 Males and Females cells and the 1913 percentage cell are written as \"—\".",
        "1916 Females printed 285,568 (same digits as the 1916 Males 515,568 tail); kept as printed.",
        "Total increase 83,693 = 811,556 - 727,863 (checks). Percentages 5.6+2.8+1.8+1.2 = 11.4, printed 11.5; kept as printed.",
        "Not totalled: 1915-17 male+female do not equal printed totals (e.g. 1915: 508,335+282,910=791,245 vs 789,123); kept as printed.",
